<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amasis II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 526 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Ahmose II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amasis II was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> from 570 to 526 BCE, of the Twenty-sixth Dynasty. A general who took the throne after an army revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apries">Apries</a>, he ruled prosperously, allied with Greek states and gave Greek merchants the trading town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naucratis">Naucratis</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> conquered Egypt months after his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amasis-ii.jpg" alt="Amasis II" width="320" height="276" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osama Shukir Muhammed Amin FRCP(Glasg) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Head_of_Amasis_II,_c._550_BCE._From_Egypt._Neues_Museum,_Berlin,_Germany.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
